  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1023 PM CDT THU OCT 29 2026\n\nThe ridging that has been in place over the Southeastern CONUS\nthe last few days is expected to slowly shift eastward as a\nshortwave trough move through the Southern Plains on Friday. Rain-\nfree conditions should continue through the day on Friday with\nincreasing high clouds as the shortwave approaches from the west.\nBy Saturday, and especially Saturday night, we'll start to see\nincreasing rain chances, especially in the evening and overnight\ninto Sunday morning. Currently, some of the higher resolution\nguidance has tried to trend lower on the rain chances compared to\nthe previous days, so that will be something to monitor during\nthe day on Friday. Otherwise, the shortwave is expected to slowly\nlift northeastward through the day on Sunday, leaving at least\nlow chances for rain through Sunday evening.\n\nWe should have dry conditions again by Monday and potentially\ninto Tuesday morning as a deeper trough begins to move through\nthe Central Plains. This system will lead to another round of\nincreased rain chances towards the middle part of next week with\nmodel guidance in decent agreement with the timing on Wednesday\ninto Thursday. However, the overall synoptic setup still has some\nuncertainty with it, so that will be monitored in the coming\ndays.\n\n25/Owen",
